In re to all the "power and frequency of named weapons and wishes" threads, 
here's my $0.02...

-Monster-specific named weapons could be more powerful against their monster 
 type.  Maybe triple damage.  A little bonus (just +1 perhaps) against all 
 monsters mightn't be a bad idea.  (I think this has already been suggested).

-Gods might still give out named weapons, but only _Very Rarely_.  Maybe one 
 when you become Hand of Elbereth/whatever else for other alignments.  They 
 might be more generous than this with minor (eg, monster-specific) named 
 weapons.

-Instead of making wishes rarer (as some people might argue you often _need_ 
 access to them to win the game), why not introduce a cost (a la D&D).
 Maybe 1 point of constitution per wish, permanent, not restorable even 
 with unicorn horns?  Maybe a luck penalty would be a good/better idea.

-Perhaps Excalibur through fountains should be available only to knights.
 (It's pretty hard for other classes to get it as it stands).  It's a 
 pretty powerful weapon, and it seems a pity to give it to just any lawful 
 character with a long sword for doing nothing special.  Knights are 
  a)  Suited for Excalibur in terms of character
  b)  Otherwise relatively weak, so they deserve an extra advantage.
 To make it still harder, perhaps impose a stricter alignment
   requirement?  Only those who have sufficient alignment to be allowed
   on their quests should be given Excalibur.

-If people really want the other named weapons, make them _sweat_ for them!
 Perhaps for each (or many) of the powerful ones (Mojo, Stormy, FireBrand
 and FrostBrand, Vorpal Blade, and Magicbane;  am I missing any [except 
 Excalibur, which I don't think should be included) should start in the 
 posession of specially designed poweful unique monsters (a mini-quest 
 might be associated with each).

    E.g.:
    Magicbane--The Sorceress
    Frost Brand--The Ice Prince
    Vorpal Blade--The Red Knight
    The Light Saber--Darth Vader  :-)
       etc.

 These would be optional quests--you wouldn't need to beat them to win the 
   game, but they are needed to get the truly coveted Named Weapons.  I'm 
   not sure whether they should be true side quests, or whether the 
   villains should just be randomly wandering around sufficiently low 
   levels of the Dungeon of Doom (no need to put all of them in every game).

-If non-named weapons aren't sufficient to make it through the lower levels, 
 IMHO this means the lower levels should be made easier, not the firepower 
 more common.  I do think the idea of making a chrysknife (which you can't 
 really get immediately anyway) more powerful is a good idea.  Maybe 
 midway between a 2-handed sword and the least powerful non-specific named 
 weapon?

-The idea with Stormbringer and ascending was cool.

